// tests/lang/stdlib/sus_threads.funny -- RUNTIME_PLAN.md R9. The same table
// the Ctrl-\ dump prints, as data, so a server can answer "what is everybody
// doing" over HTTP instead of somebody having to be at the terminal when it
// hangs.
//
// A row is a VM, and one thread can be running more than one: a program run
// by `funny run` is a VM inside the toolchain's own VM, and both are on this
// thread. So the count is not something to assert -- the shape is.
gimme sus
gimme stash

yo rows = sus.threads()
yap what_is_it(rows)
yap how_thicc(rows) >= 1

yo row = rows[how_thicc(rows) - 1]
yap what_is_it(row)
yap stash.sort(row.keys())
yap what_is_it(row["id"])
yap what_is_it(row["doing"])
yap row["intern"]
